{"archetypes":[{"name":"scope-anchor-flow","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff threads a new staged scope anchor through many plan-review surfaces where integration drift is likely.","prompt_body":"Trace the staged scope-anchor lifecycle across plan-review-loop, scout, reviewer panel, voter dispatch, revise, run-step3, and the design skill handoff. Check that brainstorm-expanded context never becomes the binding scope and that the design session feature source wins over stale implement-session state. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"marker-pipeline","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The scope-reduction marker must survive detector normalization, dedup, aggregation, tally, and renumbering without special threshold changes.","prompt_body":"Inspect the leading scope-reduction marker detector and every caller that preserves or classifies marked findings. Pay special attention to severity-prefix normalization, inline-code and fenced-code false positives, tagged-versus-untagged dedup, plan-mode aggregation fallback, and final FINDING or OOS renumbering. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"prompt-boundaries","focus_area":"security","weight":1,"rationale":"Several prompt renderers now inline untrusted issue or context text and rely on escaping, redaction, and framing.","prompt_body":"Review prompt construction changes that inline scope anchors or external context into reviewer, voter, revise, and subprocess prompts. Look for prompt-injection boundary breaks, insufficient escaping or redaction, unsafe delimiter handling, and mismatches between documentation and rendered text. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"env-handoff","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"SCOPE_ANCHOR_FILE is added to durable result-state plumbing where missing allowlist entries or unsafe values can silently break fallback behavior.","prompt_body":"Follow SCOPE_ANCHOR_FILE through inner and outer result env files, stdout breadcrumbs, phase-driver helpers, early exits, and MainAgent fallback refresh paths. Verify CR and LF rejection, path staging assumptions, allowlist updates, and preservation when result state is rewritten. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"bash-portability","focus_area":"code-quality","weight":1,"rationale":"The change adds substantial shell, awk, sed, jq, trap, and array logic that must remain portable in the repo's shell environment.","prompt_body":"Review new and modified shell scripts for Bash 3.2 compatibility, quoting, array expansion, trap cleanup, mktemp usage, jq or awk portability, and failure behavior under set -euo pipefail. Include the new plan-block, marker, voter, aggregation, and reporting scripts where relevant. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"run-summary-metrics","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff adds PR line-count reporting outside the main plan-review scope, crossing gh API, cached state, and final report rendering.","prompt_body":"Inspect the PR line-count feature across compute-pr-line-counts, write-final-report, render-run-summary, and their harnesses. Check gh API endpoint behavior, invalid or missing PR handling, cache invalidation by PR number, numeric validation, larch-logs classification, and non-fatal degradation. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
